<header class="header-section ">
<div class="intro-header no-img">
  <div class="container-md">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-xl-8 offset-xl-2 col-lg-10 offset-lg-1">
        <div class="page-heading">
          <h1>Coverage</h1>
              <hr class="small">
              <span class="page-subheading">Historical coverage of exchanges and pairs</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</header>
<div class=" container-md " role="main">
  <div class="row">
    <div class=" col-xl-10 offset-xl-1 col-lg-10 offset-lg-1 ">
      <ul>
  <li>we provide detailed data for the top 10+ tokens by market capitalization and 50+ selected smaller tokens</li>
  <li>we have 100+ pairs of detailed data (including order books) at the moment</li>
  <li>we have 1 minute candle data, open interests and funding rates for all Binance USDT futures pairs</li>
  <li>
<em>trades</em> and <em>candles</em> for all of those have coverage of about 99.7% of the time, <em>book</em> data have about 98%</li>
  <li>data from the current day are not available</li>
  <li>perpetuals/futures data have ‘-PERP’ suffix in their symbol name</li>
  <li>last days trades and order book data are uploaded every day around 01:15 UTC, the remaining data types (candles, level_1, OI, funding and more) are generated in the next couple of hours.</li>
  <li>token pairs are being added to our database incrementally, not from the first day they were listed on given exchange</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="available-history">Available history</h2>
<p>The following table contains the first dates of data in our database per exchange and data type. Other data types follow the same coverage as their closest counterpart in this table, eg. <em>level_1</em> data have the same coverage as <em>book</em> data. This does not mean that every altcoin trading pair has coverage since that date. If you’re interested only in a single pair, feel free to <a href="/contact/">ask us</a>.</p>
